                <pb facs="0843" n="836" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg836"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/11812: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-27T10:00:00+08:00">December 27, 1937—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 27—1:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>107. Was informed last night that German Ambassador presented Generalissimo
                    yesterday with a note conveying terms understood to be very drastic from
                    Japanese military. I understand terms will be published by Foreign Office today
                    or tomorrow.</p>
                <p>Sent to Shanghai. Shanghai please repeat to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
